cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Rhino Open AI Kit, please cite it as below. It was made with generative AI; see the README's 'Credits and AI disclosure'."
type: software
title: "Rhino Open AI Kit: an offline, open-source AI assistant for Rhino 8"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: MIT
authors:
  - name: "Rhino Open AI Kit contributors"
abstract: >-
  Portable, offline chat assistant for Rhino 8 on Mac and Windows. An open-weight language model
  runs locally in llama.cpp and acts on the Rhino document through tools: it reads the scene,
  writes Rhino Python using a tested helper library, and runs it after user confirmation as one
  undo step. Machine tiers from 8 GB to 128 GB with matching model presets. Developed with
  generative AI assistance (Claude, Anthropic).
keywords:
  - Rhino
  - Rhinoceros 3D
  - local AI
  - llama.cpp
  - architecture
  - computational design
references:
  - type: software
    title: "Rhinoceros 8 / RhinoCommon"
    authors:
      - name: "Robert McNeel & Associates"
    url: "https://www.rhino3d.com/"
  - type: software
    title: "llama.cpp"
    authors:
      - name: "Georgi Gerganov and contributors"
    url: "https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp"
  - type: software
    title: "Claude"
    authors:
      - name: Anthropic
    year: 2026
    url: "https://www.anthropic.com/claude"
    notes: "Large language model; wrote code and texts for Rhino Open AI Kit."
